---
args: { submission: ExpenseSubmission, caseFile: ExpenseCaseFile | null }
returns: ExpenseDispositionReview
---
Bind prior to the supplied immutable-history case file or a complete empty file at revision zero with empty originalClaimIds, components, decisions, requests, appeals, reimbursementOperationIds and paymentReceipts. Bind appeal = identifyReceiptLineage(submission, prior). Link a resubmitted receipt to its original claim and reimbursement operation; a new upload alone does not create a second reimbursable claim.

Bind components = separateReceiptComponents(submission.receiptFolders, prior.components). Preserve exact amounts, currency and dates, including separate tax, tip and fee lines. Retain unreadable values instead of reconstructing them. For each affected component call interpretBusinessShare(component, submission, appeal), collecting the returned purpose shares by componentKey into shares. Use only explicit trip, attendance and allocation facts. A personal companion does not make the claimant's supported business portion ineligible. For each affected component and its actual purpose share call evaluateDatedExpenseRule(component, share, submission.policyEditions, submission.receiptFolders), collecting the returned decisions by componentKey into decisions. Preserve the policy effective-date rule across the trip and apply an exception only to its authorized night, category, amount and person.

Bind questions = minimizeClaimantQuestions(decisions, components, submission.receiptFolders). Reuse evidence already supplied, group questions sharing one factual answer, and request sensitive material through restricted channels. A persuasive explanation without exception authority remains held. Bind independentReviewer = findIndependentExpenseReviewer(submission, decisions). If the manager is also claimant or preparer, route to the actual independent delegation; missing authority blocks payment release.

Bind nextFile: ExpenseCaseFile = { revision: advance only when receipt lineage, component versions, affected line decisions, requests or a new evidence-backed appeal changed; otherwise preserve prior.revision, originalClaimIds: preserve originals and append appeal.originalClaimId only when it is a genuinely new claim, components: merge by stable componentKey while retaining source-version lineage, decisions: preserve every prior decision outside appeal.reconsideredComponents and replace only those reconsidered by new evidence, requests: retain unresolved prior requests and close only those answered by supplied evidence, appeals: append appeal once by appealId and retain all earlier revisions, reimbursementOperationIds: prior identities unchanged because no new reimbursement operation is authorized here, paymentReceipts: prior actual receipt IDs unchanged because this submission supplies no payment receipt }. Bind duplicatePaymentBlockers by comparing the linked original claim and its reimbursement operation against prior.reimbursementOperationIds and prior.paymentReceipts; retain any uncertain match as a blocker rather than opening a second claim.

Bind reviewBlockers to unresolved receipt lineage, unreadable amounts/currency/date, policy or exception gaps, held component amounts, duplicate-payment uncertainty, missing independent reviewer, unanswered restricted evidence requests, missing independent approval, or absent current payment authorization. Bind paymentReleaseAllowed = true only if every affected amount is exactly reconciled in one authorized currency/scale, no amount remains held, duplicate-reimbursement identity is cleared, an independent approver is authorized and current approval/receipt evidence is present; this operation itself supplies no new approval or payment receipt, so it cannot claim a new payment release. Bind claimantExplanation to each affected component's actual allowed/rejected/held decision and cited rule; preserve prior explanations for unaffected claims. Return { caseFile: nextFile, claimantExplanation, questions, independentReviewer, paymentReleaseAllowed, reviewBlockers } as ExpenseDispositionReview. Never modify the original claim to match a reduced disposition.
